.el .ds Aq '
.TH tomat 1  "tomat 2.11.0" 
.SH NAME
tomat \- A Pomodoro timer with daemon support for waybar
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtomat\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tomat is a Pomodoro timer with a daemon\-based architecture, designed for seamless integration with waybar and other status bars. It uses a Unix socket for client\-server communication, ensuring your timer state persists across waybar restarts and system suspend/resume.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tomat\-daemon(1)
Manage the background daemon
.TP
tomat\-start(1)
Start a new Pomodoro session
.TP
tomat\-stop(1)
Stop the current session
.TP
tomat\-status(1)
Get current timer status
.TP
tomat\-watch(1)
Continuously output status updates
.TP
tomat\-skip(1)
Skip to the next phase
.TP
tomat\-pause(1)
Pause the current timer
.TP
tomat\-resume(1)
Resume a paused timer
.TP
tomat\-toggle(1)
Toggle timer pause/resume
.TP
tomat\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:

    # Start daemon and begin a session
    tomat daemon start
    tomat start

    # Custom session durations
    tomat start \-\-work 45 \-\-break 15

    # Check status (outputs JSON for waybar)
    tomat status

    # Toggle pause/resume
    tomat toggle

For more information, visit: https://github.com/jolars/tomat
